# oracle: fix npt/body with independent x and y barostats (no couple, the example has couple xy) and pair body/rounded/polygon, from examples/body/in.squares cut down: 2x2 replicate of data.squares, velocity create 0.5 with rot yes, mu 0.1, c_n 1, c_t 1, delta_ua 0.5, 800 steps (the example runs 100000). Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): engine vs native max relative error 7.1e-12 (pxx, step 600) over the thermo rows to step 800. Past about step 850 a contact choice flips (the single-contact friction with near-equal overlaps in this symmetric lattice) and the runs separate (1e-3 by step 1000), so the case stops at 800.
# oracle-inputs: w111body_squares.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
units           lj
dimension       2
atom_style      body rounded/polygon 1 6
atom_modify     map array
read_data       w111body_squares.data
replicate       2 2 1
velocity        all create 0.5 980411 dist gaussian mom yes rot yes
pair_style      body/rounded/polygon 1 1 0.1 0.5 0.5
pair_coeff      * * 100 2
comm_modify     vel yes
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all npt/body temp 0.5 0.5 1.0 x 0.001 0.1 1.0 y 0.001 0.1 1.0 fixedpoint 0 0 0
fix             2 all enforce2d
thermo_style    custom step pe ke etotal press pxx pyy pxy
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          100
run             800
